# =============================================================================
# WHAT MUST NOT ENTER THE IMAGE
# =============================================================================
# A build context is copied wholesale before any COPY runs, and anything a layer
# captures is permanent: it survives `docker rm`, it is pushed to the registry,
# and it cannot be un-set by editing an environment variable. So the env files -
# which in this repository are committed and contain live-looking
# credentials - are excluded here, first, by name.
#
# deploy/Dockerfile ALSO deletes them in a RUN step. That is deliberate
# duplication: this file is the mechanism, that step is the assertion, and the
# assertion catches the case where this file is stale or the build is run from a
# different context.

# ---- credentials and configuration ------------------------------------------
# Every service is started with dotenv_config_path=local.env (dev.env / prod.env
# are the other two names in use). NONE of them belongs in an image: in
# production the configuration comes from Railway's environment variables.
*.env
**/*.env
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
# The templates are documentation, not configuration, but the image does not
# need documentation either.
*.env.example
**/*.env.example

# Key material. .gitignore already blocks these from git; block them from the
# build context too, so a key sitting untracked in a working tree cannot be
# baked into a layer.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.csr
*.p12
*.pfx
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
private/

# ---- things that would make the image enormous or wrong ---------------------
# node_modules is installed inside the builder for the right platform. Copying
# the developer's macOS/arm64 tree in would ship native modules compiled for the
# wrong OS.
node_modules
**/node_modules

.git
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store

# Local database and cache state - gigabytes of it, and none of it is the app.
mongodb-data*/
**/mongodb-data*/
dump.rdb
**/dump.rdb
*.rdb
appendonly.aof
mongodb.log*
**/mongodb.log*

# Logs
*.log
**/*.log
logs/

# ---- not part of the backend ------------------------------------------------
# The frontend is a separate Railway service (a Next.js app); this image is the
# three backends only.
cryptodex-frontend/
advanced-charts/
system-smoke-test/

# Tests, coverage and build output. The runtime never reads them.
**/tests/
**/__tests__/
**/coverage/
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/playwright-report/
**/test-results/
**/jest.config.js
**/jest.setup.js
**/babel.config.js
**/.babelrc

# Local tooling that is not the deployed app
start-all.sh
stop-all.sh
.claude/

# NOTE ON ops/ - it is deliberately NOT excluded.
# ops/reset-and-seed.mjs is how a venue is brought from nothing to something
# that can fill an order (it is the only thing that writes redis
# admin_liquidity/liquidation, without which spot cannot fill at all). Keeping
# it in the image means the production databases can be seeded with
# `railway run --service backend node ops/reset-and-seed.mjs`, from inside the
# private network - instead of having to expose Mongo and Redis to the public
# internet just to run a one-off script. It resolves its mongodb/redis drivers
# out of userapi/node_modules, which the image already has.
# Its own scratch data is excluded by the rules above; what is left is ~100 KB.
